Since HyperExecute runs on remote infrastructure, you'll need the Healenium backend accessible from there. Two options: run the Docker containers on a shared server your HyperExecute agents can reach, or use the Healenium Proxy approach instead of the direct dependency approach — Healenium offers two distinct approaches: Healenium-Proxy and Healenium-Web. Healenium acts as a proxy between client and Selenium server. The proxy mode might work better with HyperExecute since it sits between your tests and the Selenium grid without requiring code changes at all. 
