What Healenium Will and Won't Fix For You
Will fix (your 60-70% of flakiness):
Element ID/name/class changed between sprints
XPath broke because DOM structure shifted
CSS selector invalidated by a redesign
Any NoSuchElementException where the element still exists but with different attributes
Won't fix (your remaining 30%):
Timeout issues (element is just slow to load)
Element exists but is behind a modal/spinner/overlay
StaleElementReferenceException from page reloads
Data-dependent failures (wrong test data)
ElementClickInterceptedException (something else covering the button)
That remaining 30% is what Phase 2 (the smart retry utility) and Phase 3 (the Copilot agent) are for. But Phase 1 with Healenium alone gives you a dramatic, demo-able improvement with essentially one line of code changed and a Docker container running.

